1) When the API container is accessing data from mongodb running on the host,
   it needs to know which IP address to use. To find the IP address of mongodb,
   use the following command on the host and place the value in conf/config.json
   under the "host_ip" property:

   $ ss -natp  | grep 27017 | grep LISTEN


2) When the API container needs to run a command from within another container,
   such as the "running_substructure", it needs to know the API url of "running_substructure",
   which is set under glygen/conf/config.json under the "jobinfo" property. To identify the
   IP address of "running_substructure", run the following command:

   $ docker exec -it running_substructure ip addr | grep inet | grep eth0



